3.1    Data Collection and Pre-processing
                                           AT
       信




      After listing related policies for the government of the United Republic of Tanzania,
we need to build models to quantify the benefits of these policies. Therefore, we first
      微

                                     M



obtained the IWT data of Tanzania in previous years from the official website of CITES
(the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora)
                             ：




and pre-processed them.
                      号




      CITES is an international agreement between governments. According to its website
[4], its aim is to ensure that international trade in specimens of wild animals and plants
               信




does not threaten the survival of the species. This website provides a database of all the
endangered species trade conducted by participating parties over the years. However,
       微




this raw data is constrained by inconsistency in units and lack of sorting, making direct
utilization impractical and requiring pre-processing.

      To enhance our model’s utilization of data, we pre-processed the data and obtained
the total trade volume for each term in Tanzania annually. Due to potential inconsistencies
in units between different terms (e.g., kg and unknown), we perform minimax normal-
