7 Policy Impacts in a Larger Complex System
                                    ：

                                                              els
                                   号
7.1    IWT and Climate Change




                                                            od
                            众

      There has been previous literature on the damage of wildlife crime to the global cli-
                                                           m
mate change. Thus our policies will have a positive impact on slowing down the path of
                    公


global climate change while reducing illegal wildlife trade.
                                               H
      First, the transportation of IWT generates a large amount of carbon emissions, mainly
                                            AT
       信




due to transports. We will reduce the transportation demand of IWT, and then reduce
carbon emissions generated during transportation.
      微

                                      M


      Second, wildlife plays an important role against climate change. As producers in the
ecosystem, plants absorb carbon dioxide in the atmosphere through photosynthesis and
                             ：




have a part in carbon sequestration. While wild animals are consumers, past research
has shown that protecting and restoring wildlife can enhance natural carbon capture and
                      号




sequestration, even capturing up to 95% of the carbon needed to achieve goals of The Paris
Agreement each year[23]. Our policies reduce the decline in wildlife populations caused
              信




by poaching, enhancing carbon capture and sequestration.

      Finally, the massive illegal wildlife trade destroys biodiversity, which in turn jeopar-
       微




dizes the global climate. Wildlife trade significantly reduces species richness and increases
the risk of extinction of traded species[19]. Meanwhile, IPBE and IPCC has shown the
deep links between biodiversity and climate change[8]. Our policies protect biodiversity
by reducing poaching, and then plays a positive part in mitigating global climate change.

